{
  "comment": [
    "UNION ALL phase 5: ordering a set operation by its own output columns.",
    "",
    "Eight classes. Five attack what this phase introduced — which names may be",
    "ordered by, that a name carried twice is refused, and that a direction and a",
    "second term survive from the declaration to the statement. Three attack compiler",
    "rules ordering is the first thing to make reachable or to make matter: the fixed",
    "order of a compound's trailing clauses, and the parentheses that keep a nested",
    "operation's clauses its own.",
    "",
    "Two of them, P5-3 and P5-4, are the same observable failure from two different",
    "causes — the direction lost where the term is built, and lost where it is",
    "written. They share a killer and have different probes, because a repair to one",
    "is not evidence about the other.",
    "",
    "Every site names the function it is inside, which the harness checks. Three",
    "probes in this batch were first aimed at a function the mutation did not touch,",
    "and the campaign refused the classes rather than recording them; naming the",
    "function makes the level something the author writes down instead of assumes.",
    "",
    "Kept apart from the other five manifests, whose accounting is closed. UNION ALL",
    "is not frozen and this is not the UNION manifest.",
    "",
    "Every killer runs in the root module and needs no database, so this campaign",
    "reproduces on any machine whatever ports are free. Whether the rows actually",
    "come back in order is a question only a server can answer, and it is answered in",
    "internal/gendemo/m16_unionorder_test.go."
  ],
  "evidence_commit": "ab3e1df",
  "evidence_commit_note": [
    "ab3e1df is the revision every UNION ALL class was last applied to and run at, in a",
    "worktree checked out at exactly that commit, with the manifests read and written",
    "outside it so the tree stayed clean between classes. It is kept reachable as",
    "archive/m16-union-mutation-evidence.",
    "",
    "The five UNION ALL campaigns were rerun together at one revision after `mutate",
    "anchors` found four anchors that later phases had silently invalidated by editing",
    "the code they quote. An anchor that no longer matches makes its class look like a",
    "survivor, so the campaigns were pinned to revisions where they no longer ran.",
    "They run again, and three harness controls were active: anchors still quote their",
    "code, every site names the function its anchor is inside, and each semantic probe",
    "survives every mutation in another function."
  ],
  "not_expressible": [
    {
      "id": "P5-8",
      "name": "An ambiguous ordering term is accepted",
      "why": [
        "This was a class, and it was caught. It is now not expressible, which is a",
        "better outcome than catching it.",
        "",
        "It attacked a check in the ordering path that refused a name two result",
        "columns carry. The check existed because the rule lived at the consumers of",
        "a shape's name list, and one of four consumers had not asked. The rule moved",
        "to where the shape is built: a shape is refused unless its names identify its",
        "columns, so no consumer receives one that does not, and the check in the",
        "ordering path was removed as a guard on a state that cannot occur.",
        "",
        "There is now no mutation that reaches the defect. Removing the shape's rule",
        "is a different class about a different function, and its own killers are the",
        "five consumers that inherit it. The precondition subtest kept under this id",
        "asserts the state stays unreachable, so a change that made it reachable again",
        "would ask for the class back."
      ]
    }
  ],
